{"key":"7d7cecfbc8324b33","source_file":"Potts Mi - My.json","source_id":16088,"source_url":"concordance-mock-at-ppl-subsannare","term":"Mock at","headwords":["Mock at","Mocker","Mockery"],"latin":["Subsannare","Subsannator","Subsannatio"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Mock at"],"latin":["Subsannare"]},{"english":["Mocker"],"latin":["Subsannator"]},{"english":["Mockery"],"latin":["Subsannatio"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE","DP","HH","SE"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"1877","subsection":"2"},"text":"They mock at the things which are of the internal sense of the Word. AC 9407:4.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"2126","subsection":"end"},"text":"They mocked at this reply.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"5022","subsection":"2"},"text":"If what is internal or spiritual is mentioned, they ridicule it...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"5719","subsection":null},"text":"They who despise and ridicule the Word in the letter...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6907","subsection":"2"},"text":"Whenever they hear anyone professing the truths of the Church... they mock in themselves...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"7332","subsection":"end"},"text":"If the truths of doctrine did not serve them as means for gain, they would mock at them.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"7665","subsection":null},"text":"A mockery. Signified.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"9348","subsection":"7"},"text":"From the love of self spring... the derision and vituperation of others... In the other life... they deride the Word.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"HH","section":"506","subsection":"2"},"text":"In the other life... from their evil cupidities they burst out... into mockeries and blasphemies.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"HH","section":"575","subsection":null},"text":"The gnashing of teeth is the continual disputing of falsities... conjoined with... mockery, etc.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DP","section":"208","subsection":"end"},"text":"All are... deriders of the Divine Providence.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"5138","subsection":null},"text":"Concerning mockers, hypocrites.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"654","subsection":"55"},"text":"This is their derision in the land of Egypt () = the vituperation of doctrine from the natural man, and the contempt of the latter.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"778","subsection":"12"},"text":"Under Blaspheme, see this reference.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"mock-at-7d7cec","url":"/meta/potts/mock-at-7d7cec/"}